{"title":"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(a_bit_of_trigonometry)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (a bit of trigonometry)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(trig_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (trig bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A regular octagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> has sides of length two.  Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b22de7a6a4a849d8997f3db62b129ea8c74b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADG$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/5/4a59de5cfea6537885df98a7dad9c00a2226539b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 4 + 2\\sqrt2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 6 + \\sqrt2\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 4 + 3\\sqrt2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 3 + 4\\sqrt2 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 8 + \\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"613\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca90d855ac2876463b79d50db160c0d88e6f0f30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair[] A = new pair[8]; A[0]=(0,0); for (int i=1; i&lt;8; ++i) A[i] = A[i-1] + 2*dir(45*(i-1)); draw( A[0]--A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--A[5]--A[6]--A[7]--cycle ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A[0],SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,A[1],SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,A[2],SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,A[3],NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,A[4],NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,A[5],NW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,A[6],NW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,A[7],SW); filldraw( A[0]--A[3]--A[6]--cycle, lightgray, black ); pair P = intersectionpoint( A[3]--A[6], A[0]--A[5] ); draw( A[0]--P ); draw( P -- A[5], dashed ); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,NE); draw( A[1]--A[4], dashed ); pair Q = intersectionpoint( A[3]--A[6], A[1]--A[4] ); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,NW); [/asy]\" width=\"278\" height=\"272\" />\n</p><p>The area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c11c783ddf150fb2c99ce6dd035d42bbaa7e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADG$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> can be computed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/30332448459c106124db07d6eaeb1b6615d843af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DG \\cdot AP}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />. We will now find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/f/eaf9409044fef7f3966027eec40b2cced52eb16c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DG$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e775199b80d4ef43c1bc7b0a4302325ae4a974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PFG$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is a right isosceles triangle with hypotenuse of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/a/2ba7dd3572fb3ac89291d72d7a0de21e54482e83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PG=\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. \nThe same holds for triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/4965e3d73b33f66d3c40556be29a9ccdae238e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> and its leg <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe3f0862fc765c6a4384b9fd9e0182b086f06a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" />. The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42cf1079fd4f9e6ee61b1b7fe39a0cab5a6c8738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=2$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />.\nHence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c758ac2851027af3370c40ab176671caed1b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD = 2 + 2\\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/7/3d702a7f949b9babeda91824279fce7d547bc445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = PD = 2 + \\sqrt 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c11c783ddf150fb2c99ce6dd035d42bbaa7e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADG$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/56272cec170ff636b205ca8f09d27575c74d9a9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DG \\cdot AP}2 = \\frac{(2+2\\sqrt 2)(2+\\sqrt 2)}2 = \\frac{8+6\\sqrt 2}2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}=4+3\\sqrt 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"498\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28a_bit_of_trigonometry.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(a_bit_of_trigonometry)\">Solution 2 (a bit of trigonometry)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (a bit of trigonometry)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(Refer to diagram above)\n</p><p>Notice how the area of triangle is equivalent to the area of the octagon minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b20ab3b93c0d5fbde4dfe7f25d37e90fd06512a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A_{ABCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" /> and then minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a968847cf7afb80d8264a126841a0dd5370d7c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{\\triangle AHG}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>THe trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles trapezoid. It can be broken apart into a rectangle, and two right triangles. These triangles are isosceles, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/9/2298dd4358fbefe327f52d37a93f9a5535148b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GFP = \\angle GFE - \\angle PFE = 135^{\\circ} - 90^{\\circ} = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"373\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a4d9f60adf51b97b2ebb2c0303ac60a587500e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(45^{\\circ}) = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"117\" height=\"43\" />, so the legs of the isosceles right triangles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. The area of the trapezoid can be calculated as followed:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/63970251ee0e78018f243f8a51bf804bb2ee3f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{PQEF} + 2A_{GFP} = 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{2} + 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{2}^2 \\div 2 = 2\\sqrt{2}+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"401\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>The area formula for a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfdeb2d535fc4c75acdc21f48a2bc53381759df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the included angle between sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />. Using this for triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44025d179650d65e4da46151a9dec32db4423c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AHG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01de13a7a88549f516d16193eec14a4e6b0dbac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 \\cdot \\sin(135)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/4308937dc8d3b286dc10ac82169af99379dac663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(135) = \\sin(90+45) = \\sin(90)\\cos(45) + \\cos(90)\\sin(45) = 1 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} + 0 \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"660\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, the area of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44025d179650d65e4da46151a9dec32db4423c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AHG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>The total area between two times the trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/0/44025d179650d65e4da46151a9dec32db4423c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AHG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/b/2cb408b575155f837ffbed155babc8a53334b89b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\sqrt{2}+4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />. The area of the octagon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f027ace8d4a3622d167d0f36ba3cf852d28967c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(1+\\sqrt{2}) \\cdot 2^2 = 8 + 8\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"199\" height=\"24\" />. Subtracting the areas, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24a7af830c3aae8e1f32aa66d9447e0c35c63a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+3\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/b/82b317654f901a9c8f56585721a617396d3b050c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28trig_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(trig_bash)\">Solution 3 (trig bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (trig bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befd32d2276afa604d385a389d1099b9c7e9b29c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(1cm); defaultpen(0.8); pair[] A = new pair[8]; A[0]=(0,0); for (int i=1; i&lt;8; ++i) A[i] = A[i-1] + 2*dir(45*(i-1)); draw( A[0]--A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--A[5]--A[6]--A[7]--cycle ); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A[0],SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,A[1],SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,A[2],SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,A[3],NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,A[4],NE); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,A[5],NW); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,A[6],NW); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,A[7],SW); filldraw( A[0]--A[3]--A[6]--cycle, lightgray, black );  pair M = midpoint(A[0]--A[6]); draw( A[7]--M, dashed ); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, S);  pair R1 = extension(A[4],A[5],A[6],A[7]); pair R2 = extension(A[4],A[5],A[3],A[2]); draw( A[5]--R1, dashed ); draw( A[4]--R2, dashed ); draw( A[7]--R1, dashed ); draw( A[2]--R2, dashed ); label(&quot;$I$&quot;, R1, N); label(&quot;$J$&quot;, R2, N); [/asy]\" width=\"278\" height=\"272\" />\nWe are trying to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b22de7a6a4a849d8997f3db62b129ea8c74b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADG$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> by using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfdeb2d535fc4c75acdc21f48a2bc53381759df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" /> and using sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2e9f77cf5375d42ace718f4059234d9eb51230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We note that the angle HGM is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529877bdfd249af50c932213d1e66581b2a1fcab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"32\" height=\"40\" />. We need to find the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> Then we recall the half angle identity:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9ff8dc3d011863c27bbaa37e0ebfe87b9cb5533.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(\\theta)}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"193\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Then by substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/836de22e20f4d79b9a6d1c56368c83cc830d7c57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(45^\\circ) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"119\" height=\"43\" /> into the identity above, we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49bd02580f73a2c71e3f9aba9d5f728e58c8beb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\cos(45/2)^\\circ}{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos(45)}{2}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}}{2}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2\\sqrt{2}}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"578\" height=\"59\" />\n</p><p>The length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/a/faa955526ea1e9abc183de36b8bd8097786ed5b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} = 4 \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"234\" height=\"56\" />. We will leave this without simplifying. \n</p><p>Now we find the length of GD.\n</p><p>In the diagram above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2a3fbd489f8cb49b097256c035d644e0534575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle IFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68abb96c96f6f54e4746584be111086b7a3ffa4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle JED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> are isosceles right triangles. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71a06b0e91cdadfeaeb94608ac3cdfbf1897d4d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF = EJ = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"177\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450b8ef8ef4e1576d76f2d7d1e16bf005f0646b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD = IJ = IF + FE + EJ = \\sqrt{2} + 2 + \\sqrt{2} = 2 + 2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"453\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Now we have the lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/1/b11fca7fa0396390456782405b2897976a413f77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/2/de2e9f77cf5375d42ace718f4059234d9eb51230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, we still have one step left: finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c136ef57b0501b5e9caedb16dbc5015f43a6fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(\\angle AGD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a101a33f930ff6f90a5a2b4d2e6bf8c6a2448f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGD =(90 - \\angle HGM)^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"208\" height=\"20\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fdba8230aa4e7b68c887b9f3a4f54feb1261393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DGH = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" />. We already found <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb5104ff124252fdb117569054c1bd70a9a843d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HGM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/9/529877bdfd249af50c932213d1e66581b2a1fcab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45}{2}^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"32\" height=\"40\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfbf38d51b340d37e63f0d4890b7c17426f5fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AGD =(90 - \\frac{45}{2})^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"167\" height=\"38\" />. Now we can find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b22de7a6a4a849d8997f3db62b129ea8c74b4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADG$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> \n</p><p>Substituting our values into the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfdeb2d535fc4c75acdc21f48a2bc53381759df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" />, we get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969d0d3ef9568f3fd0f44e58daab3e6ca6c37cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Area of } \\triangle ADG = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sin\\left((90-\\tfrac{45}{2})^{\\circ}\\right) \\cdot 4\\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\cdot (2 + 2\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"483\" height=\"56\" /> \n</p><p>Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fbece828e035b3d3a88257f471bb704e9b0de12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin(90^\\circ - x) = \\cos(x), \\quad \\sin\\left((90-\\tfrac{45}{2})^{\\circ}\\right) = \\cos\\left(\\tfrac{45}{2}^\\circ\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"408\" height=\"24\" />. \n</p><p>Substituting this back into the expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a142f96b738babad72bae9fcabafcc9828173ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sin\\left((90-\\tfrac{45}{2})^{\\circ}\\right) \\cdot 4\\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\cdot (2 + 2\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"341\" height=\"56\" /> , we get \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34319f7068f132a30562cf69710fbd9def06a9da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\cos\\left(\\tfrac{45}{2}^\\circ\\right) \\cdot 4\\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\cdot (2 + 2\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\cdot 4\\sqrt{\\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4}} \\cdot (2 + 2\\sqrt{2})=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"626\" height=\"56\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45c0ae65a6d90bb9c22c6deb0b00f64728e295ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{4} \\cdot (2 + 2\\sqrt{2}) = \\frac{(2+\\sqrt{2})(2+2\\sqrt{2})}{2} =  \\frac{4 + 4\\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{2} + 4}{2} = \\frac{8 + 6\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 4 + 3\\cdot \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"727\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6dbbac62a58811f44fda1df541fe2d2b7f43bc64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>~BiegeTomcat72\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B\">2002 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002